INT. PAWNSHOP - NIGHT

Guitars on the wall. Glass cases of rings and watches. Barred windows glow with neon.

HUGO VANTERPOOL, 60s, pawnbroker, cardigan, shuffles behind the counter. He looks up as the door chime sounds.

A STRANGER, 30s, wet coat, gaunt, enters. He keeps his right hand in his pocket. He wanders to the cases.

HUGO
Help you?

STRANGER
Browsing.

HUGO
We close in ten minutes.

STRANGER
Then I'll be quick.

He stops at a case of wedding bands. Taps the glass. Hugo pays him no mind, flips through a ledger.

The door chimes again. DET. SABINE ARCHAMBAULT, 40s, trench coat, badge on her belt, steps in. She nods at Hugo. Her eyes land on the Stranger. Then slide away.

ARCHAMBAULT
Evening, Hugo.

HUGO
Detective.

ARCHAMBAULT
Anything come in today?

HUGO
A banjo. A set of knives. A ring.

ARCHAMBAULT
Which ring?

Hugo gestures at the case the Stranger is standing over. The Stranger's hand tightens in his pocket.

ARCHAMBAULT (CONT'D)
(mild)
Sir, can I see your hands?

STRANGER
Why?

ARCHAMBAULT
Humour me.

The Stranger takes out his hand. It's empty and trembling. He holds it up, palm out.

STRANGER
I'm just looking at rings.

ARCHAMBAULT
What's your name?

STRANGER
Wallace.

ARCHAMBAULT
Wallace what?

WALLACE
Teague. I live on Delancey.

ARCHAMBAULT
Mr. Teague. A woman reported her ring stolen last Friday. Gold, with a small sapphire.

Hugo pulls a velvet box from under the counter. Opens it. A gold ring with a small sapphire.

HUGO
Wallace sold me this on Saturday.

WALLACE
It was my mother's.

ARCHAMBAULT
Whose ring was it before it was your mother's?

Wallace's shoulders sag. He sits on a stool by the guitars. Puts his face in his hands.

WALLACE
I needed rent.

Archambault sighs. Takes the ring from the box. Closes her fingers around it.

ARCHAMBAULT
Hugo, keep the shop open. I'll be back with the owner.

She nods at Wallace.

ARCHAMBAULT (CONT'D)
You're coming with me.

He rises. Follows her to the door. The chime sounds as they leave. Hugo lets out a long breath and goes back to his ledger.
